        {
          "id": 3351619736,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "I think we should have all About information in the Wireshark About dialog, no special handling here. The same with the Lua Debugger Settings which should be moved to the Preferences. I'm waiting for Rolands Theme Manager before deciding how to move it.\n\nThe Lua Debugger is very close to a generic \"Lua plugin handler for Wireshark\" if we want to have this. Adding create-new, save-as, disable, delete, etc. will make it easier to handle Lua plugins. The editor may also get improved features if we want to go even further. I don't want to extend the toolbar with too many buttons because the sections will be too wide. Maybe make the toolbar also on top of the editor will help. Or split the toolbar in two, one for debugging and one for code edit.\n\nA help button should be in the toolbar, and making it point to a WSDG section should be solvable.",
          "author": {
            "id": 4753670,
            "username": "stigbjorlykke",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Stig Bjørlykke",
            "state": "active",
